<div class="hive-flow">
  <input class="motion-check" type="checkbox" id="hive-motion" />
  <label class="motion-control" for="hive-motion"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Pause animation</label>
  <div class="flow-panels">
    <figure class="flow-panel solution-design" aria-labelledby="design-heading">
      <figcaption class="panel-heading">
        <div class="heading-title"><span class="loop-number">01</span><div><p class="overline">Design the solution</p><h3 id="design-heading">Give the project a map.</h3></div></div>
        <p>Turn the solution into a plan,<br class="desktop-break" /> then connect every gateway.</p>
      </figcaption>
      <ol class="coordination-lane design-lane" aria-label="Solution design before coordination">
        <li class="flow-step gateway">
          <div class="node-card">
            <span class="node-mark gateway-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <span class="node-meta">Architecture</span><h4>Build the system design</h4><p>Define the problem, system boundaries, interfaces, and constraints.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="connector" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-step context">
          <div class="node-card">
            <span class="node-mark packet-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
            <span class="node-meta">Delivery plan</span><h4>Design the plan</h4><p>Break the solution into milestones, tasks, owners, and acceptance criteria.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="connector" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-step">
          <div class="node-card">
            <span class="node-mark graph-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <span class="node-meta">Scope + guardrails</span><h4>Connect all gateways</h4><p>Build the dependency graph across the project. Each gateway defines what is ready and what is allowed.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="return-path"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><p><strong>The graph guides the work</strong> — scope, dependencies, and acceptance travel into every assignment.</p></div>
    </figure>
    <div class="between-loops" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><p>Gateway graph + design plan</p><span>↓</span></div>
    <figure class="flow-panel" aria-labelledby="coordination-heading">
      <figcaption class="panel-heading">
        <div class="heading-title"><span class="loop-number">02</span><div><p class="overline">The coordination loop</p><h3 id="coordination-heading">One goal. Shared direction.</h3></div></div>
        <p>Define the work, give it an owner,<br class="desktop-break" /> and send the right context.</p>
      </figcaption>
      <ol class="coordination-lane" aria-label="Coordination stages in dependency order">
        <li class="flow-step gateway">
          <div class="node-card">
            <span class="node-mark gateway-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            <span class="node-meta">Coordinator</span><h4>Select the ready work</h4><p>Use the gateway graph to choose the sprint and assign tasks within scope.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="connector" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-step context">
          <div class="node-card">
            <span class="node-mark packet-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
            <span class="node-meta">Task packet</span><h4>Package the context</h4><p>Relevant contracts, files, and previous evidence.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="connector" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-step specialists">
          <div class="worker-pair">
            <div class="worker"><span class="worker-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><h4>Specialist A</h4><p>Task / worktree A</p><span class="worker-loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> Ralph executor</span></div></div>
            <div class="worker"><span class="worker-dot secondary" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><h4>Specialist B</h4><p>Task / worktree B</p><span class="worker-loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> Ralph executor</span></div></div>
          </div>
          <span class="worker-note">Up to two parallel writers</span>
          <span class="connector" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-step candidate">
          <div class="node-card">
            <span class="node-mark evidence-mark" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
            <span class="node-meta">Ready for review</span><h4>Bring the evidence</h4><p>A candidate, test results, and a clear handoff to QA.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="return-path"><span aria-hidden="true">↶</span><p><strong>Back to the gateway</strong> — the coordinator records progress and selects the next ready task.</p></div>
    </figure>
    <div class="between-loops" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><p>Inside each specialist’s task</p><span>↓</span></div>
    <figure class="flow-panel quality" aria-labelledby="quality-heading">
      <figcaption class="panel-heading">
        <div class="heading-title"><span class="loop-number">03</span><div><p class="overline">Execution &amp; review</p><h3 id="quality-heading">Ralph executes. QA reviews.</h3></div></div>
        <p>Separate responsibilities.<br class="desktop-break" /> The same task worktree.</p>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="worktree-boundary">
      <p class="worktree-label"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Same worktree / executor + independent QA</p>
      <div class="quality-layout">
        <div class="iteration">
          <p class="lane-label">Ralph loop / task executor</p>
          <ol class="iteration-lane">
            <li><span class="step-index">01</span><h4>Implement</h4><p>A focused change</p></li>
            <li><span class="step-index">02</span><h4>Test</h4><p>Check the boundary</p></li>
            <li><span class="step-index">03</span><h4>Record</h4><p>Keep the evidence</p></li>
          </ol>
          <div class="small-return"><span aria-hidden="true">↶</span> Implement → test → record → repair as needed. Send the candidate and evidence to QA when ready.</div>
        </div>
        <span class="review-connector" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
        <div class="qa-card"><span class="qa-seal" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="node-meta">Review loop</span><h4>Independent QA</h4><p>Review the candidate in this same worktree. Run acceptance, inspect the consumer, and verify the evidence.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="worktree-caption">The executor owns changes. QA reviews independently in the same worktree; a failed review returns to the executor before QA checks again.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-paths">
        <div class="decision repair"><span class="decision-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↶</span><div><span class="decision-label">FAIL / return to Ralph</span><h4>Repair → retest → QA again</h4><p>A linked fix in the same task worktree, within the graph’s scope.</p></div></div>
        <div class="decision deliver"><span class="decision-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><span class="decision-label">PASS / move forward</span><h4>Integrate → final acceptance</h4><p>Verify the target, archive the receipt, open the next gateway.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <div class="memory-note"><span class="memory-icon" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><p><strong>Graph for guardrails. Ralph for execution. QA for verification.</strong> Contracts, checkpoints, and evidence connect all three.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
